{% comment %}
  Board - what is next, the whole day beside it, and what is left of it.

  The full-panel design, so it can afford to answer more than one question at
  once: the next thing large enough to read across a room, the day drawn where
  it falls so the shape of it is visible, and the three figures that say how
  much of it is already gone.

  The countdown is worked out here against the clock at the moment of drawing,
  not taken from the payload - the payload's was true when Google was last
  asked, which is up to ten minutes ago. `tick: 300` in the manifest is the
  other half of that: the server redraws this every five minutes whether or not
  anything new was fetched.
{% endcomment %}

{%- assign day = calendar -%}
{%- assign hh = "now" | date: "%H" | times: 60 -%}
{%- assign now_mins = "now" | date: "%M" | plus: hh -%}

{%- comment %} How many are actually left, counted against the clock at the
  moment of drawing rather than taken from the payload. `today.remaining` was
  true when Google was last asked, which is up to ten minutes ago, and this
  design decides what to *say* from the live clock - so the two disagree for
  the whole of that window and the panel prints "6 left" beside "Nothing left
  today". Same reason the countdowns are worked out here. {% endcomment -%}
{%- assign left = 0 -%}
{%- for event in day.events -%}
  {%- if event.end_minutes > now_mins %}{% assign left = left | plus: 1 %}{% endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- assign gone = day.today.total | minus: left | at_least: 0 -%}

{%- assign running = false -%}
{%- assign coming = false -%}
{%- for event in day.upcoming -%}
  {%- if event.start_minutes > now_mins -%}
    {%- if coming == false %}{% assign coming = event %}{% endif -%}
  {%- elsif running == false and event.end_minutes > now_mins -%}
    {%- assign running = event -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}

{%- comment %} Out of day, but not out of calendar.
  The board has a whole panel and used to spend the best half of it on the
  words "Nothing left today" - correct, and the least useful thing on the wall
  from six o'clock until midnight. `next_any` is the next thing anywhere in the
  window that was actually fetched, so the headline stays a headline and the
  fact that today is finished moves into the chip above it. A widget asked only
  about today has nothing to reach for, and falls through to the empty branch
  below rather than inventing a tomorrow it never looked at. {% endcomment -%}
{%- assign later = false -%}
{%- if running == false and coming == false and day.next_any and day.next_any.start_minutes > now_mins -%}
  {%- comment %} Only when it is genuinely still ahead. A payload is up to ten
    minutes old, and `next_any` was the next thing when Google was last asked -
    so it has to be checked against the clock at the moment of drawing, exactly
    as the countdown is. Left unchecked, a meeting that started while nobody
    was looking is drawn as the next one with "now" beside it. {% endcomment -%}
  {%- assign coming = day.next_any -%}
  {%- comment %} "Nothing left today" only when it is genuinely not today: a
    horizon shorter than the day leaves a late meeting out of `upcoming` while
    it is still ahead of you, and that wants the ordinary countdown rather than
    an announcement that today is over. {% endcomment -%}
  {%- if day.next_any_day != "Today" %}{% assign later = true %}{% endif -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- assign open = extension.values.day_start | default: "08:00" | minutes_of -%}
{%- assign close = extension.values.day_end | default: "20:00" | minutes_of -%}
{%- for event in day.events -%}
  {%- if event.start_minutes < open -%}
    {%- assign open = event.start_minutes | divided_by: 60 | times: 60 -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if event.end_minutes > close -%}
    {%- assign close = event.end_minutes | plus: 59 | divided_by: 60 | times: 60 -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- if now_mins < open %}{% assign open = now_mins | divided_by: 60 | times: 60 %}{% endif -%}
{%- if now_mins > close %}{% assign close = now_mins | plus: 59 | divided_by: 60 | times: 60 %}{% endif -%}
{%- assign span = close | minus: open | at_least: 120 -%}

{%- assign box_h = shape.height | at_least: 300 -%}
{%- assign box_w = shape.width | at_least: 500 -%}
{%- comment %} How tall the day column actually is, which decides whether a
  block has room for its own title. The title bar and the padding come off
  first; guess high and a half-hour meeting is told it has room for two lines
  it does not have. {% endcomment -%}
{%- assign track_h = box_h | minus: 56 | minus: 28 | at_least: 120 -%}

{%- assign hours = span | divided_by: 60 -%}
{%- assign per_hour = track_h | divided_by: hours | at_least: 1 -%}
{%- assign every = 1 -%}
{%- if per_hour < 30 %}{% assign every = 2 %}{% endif -%}
{%- if per_hour < 15 %}{% assign every = 3 %}{% endif -%}
{%- assign first_hour = open | divided_by: 60 -%}
{%- assign last_hour = close | divided_by: 60 -%}
{%- assign gutter = 30 -%}

<div class="screen">
  <div class="title-bar" style="padding: 16px 24px 10px">
    <div class="title">{{ extension.values.heading | default: day.today.date }}</div>
    {%- comment %} "0 left" is arithmetic rather than news. {% endcomment -%}
    <div class="chip self-start">
      <span class="i i-calendar"></span>
      {% if left > 0 %}{{ left }} left
      {% elsif day.today.total > 0 %}all done
      {% else %}clear{% endif %}
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="content" style="padding: 14px 24px">
    <div class="split-detail">
      <div class="stack fit" style="gap: 12px">
        {%- comment %} What is next, or what you are in the middle of. {% endcomment -%}
        {% if running %}
          {%- assign left = running.end_minutes | minus: now_mins -%}
          <div class="stack stack--tight" style="gap: 6px">
            <p class="with-icon" style="gap: 8px">
              <span class="badge">Now</span>
              <span class="t-md t-bold">{{ left | at_least: 1 }} min left</span>
            </p>
            <p class="t-bold clamp-2" style="font-size: {{ box_w | divided_by: 19 | at_most: 40 | at_least: 20 }}px; line-height: 1.05">
              {{ running.title }}
            </p>
            <p class="t-md t-mono t-bold">{{ running.start }} &ndash; {{ running.end }}</p>
            {% if extension.values.show_location != false and running.location != blank %}
              <p class="with-icon t-sm">
                <span class="i i-{% if running.remote %}video{% else %}pin{% endif %} i-sm"></span>
                <span class="truncate">{{ running.location }}</span>
              </p>
            {% endif %}
          </div>
        {% elsif coming %}
          {%- assign until = coming.start_minutes | minus: now_mins -%}
          <div class="stack stack--tight" style="gap: 6px">
            {% if later %}
              <span class="chip self-start">
                <span class="i i-calendar-check"></span>Nothing left today
              </span>
            {% else %}
              <span class="chip self-start">
                <span class="i i-clock"></span>{{ until | in_words }}{% if coming.start_minutes >= 1440 %} &middot; tomorrow{% endif %}
              </span>
            {% endif %}
            <p class="t-bold clamp-2" style="font-size: {{ box_w | divided_by: 19 | at_most: 40 | at_least: 20 }}px; line-height: 1.05">
              {{ coming.title }}
            </p>
            {%- comment %} One line, always. "TOMORROW 28 AUG · 08:30 - 09:15"
              is too long for eight columns, and wrapped it pushed the whole
              stack down through the figures below it - which reads as a broken
              screen rather than as a long line. The date is the part worth
              dropping: the day name carries the meaning and the date only
              confirms it. {% endcomment -%}
            <p class="t-md t-mono t-bold truncate">
              {% if later %}<span class="t-upper">{{ day.next_any_day }}</span> &middot; {% endif %}{{ coming.start }} &ndash; {{ coming.end }}
            </p>
            {% if extension.values.show_location != false and coming.location != blank %}
              <p class="with-icon t-sm">
                <span class="i i-{% if coming.remote %}video{% else %}pin{% endif %} i-sm"></span>
                <span class="truncate">{{ coming.location }}</span>
              </p>
            {% endif %}
          </div>
        {% else %}
          {%- comment %} Nothing ahead anywhere in what was asked for. The
            column beside this is already drawing the day that has gone, so
            what belongs here is the plain news and how the day actually went -
            never "tomorrow is clear too", which a widget asked about today
            alone has no way of knowing and said every evening regardless. {% endcomment -%}
          <div class="stack stack--tight" style="gap: 6px">
            {%- comment %} Sized off the box rather than fixed at t-xl: at eight
              rows the label wraps to two lines of 36 pixels, and the column is
              a flex stack - the figures underneath do not move down out of its
              way, they are simply drawn through. {% endcomment -%}
            {% if box_h > 340 %}<span class="i i-calendar-check i-lg"></span>{% endif %}
            <p class="t-bold clamp-2" style="font-size: {{ box_w | divided_by: 22 | at_least: 18 | at_most: 36 }}px; line-height: 1.1">
              {{ day.empty_label | default: "Nothing left today" }}
            </p>
            <p class="t-sm clamp-2">
              {% if day.today.total > 0 %}
                {{ day.today.total }} of them, {{ day.today.busy_text }} in all{% if day.today.last_end != blank %}, finished at {{ day.today.last_end }}{% endif %}.
              {% elsif day.all_day.size > 0 %}
                Nothing timed. {% for entry in day.all_day %}{{ entry.title }}{% unless forloop.last %}, {% endunless %}{% endfor %}.
              {% else %}
                Nothing on it at all.
              {% endif %}
            </p>
          </div>
        {% endif %}

        {%- comment %} The three figures that say how today has actually gone -
          and where the longest hole in what is left of it is, which is the
          thing anybody looking at a calendar is really after. {% endcomment -%}
        <div class="facts fit" style="align-content: end; overflow: hidden">
          <div class="row">
            <span class="name"><span class="i i-hourglass i-xs"></span>Booked today</span>
            <span class="figure">{{ day.today.busy_text }}</span>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <span class="name"><span class="i i-calendar i-xs"></span>Meetings</span>
            <span class="figure">{{ day.today.total }}{% if gone > 0 %}, {{ gone }} done{% endif %}</span>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <span class="name"><span class="i i-check i-xs"></span>Free</span>
            <span class="figure">{{ day.today.free_text }}</span>
          </div>
          {%- comment %} The last two rows are the first things to go. At eight
            rows the column is about ten pixels over its budget, and a grid with
            `align-content: end` that has been shrunk does not clip - it draws
            upwards, through the headline above it. {% endcomment -%}
          {% if box_h > 340 and day.longest_gap and extension.values.show_gaps != false %}
            <div class="row">
              <span class="name"><span class="i i-dot i-xs"></span>Longest gap</span>
              <span class="figure">{{ day.longest_gap.from }}&ndash;{{ day.longest_gap.to }}</span>
            </div>
          {% endif %}
          {% if box_h <= 340 %}
          {% elsif day.today.conflicts > 0 %}
            <div class="row">
              <span class="name"><span class="i i-alert i-xs"></span>Double booked</span>
              <span class="figure">{{ day.today.conflicts }}</span>
            </div>
          {% elsif day.tomorrow.count > 0 %}
            <div class="row">
              <span class="name"><span class="i i-calendar i-xs"></span>Tomorrow</span>
              <span class="figure">{{ day.tomorrow.count }} &middot; from {{ day.tomorrow.first.start }}</span>
            </div>
          {% endif %}
        </div>
      </div>

      {%- comment %} The day itself, drawn where it falls. Same geometry as the
        tall design: an inset track so every percentage is a percentage of the
        track rather than of the panel. {% endcomment -%}
      <div class="fit" style="position: relative; min-height: 0">
        {% for hour in (first_hour..last_hour) %}
          {%- assign at = hour | times: 60 | minus: open | times: 1000 | divided_by: span -%}
          {%- assign since = hour | minus: first_hour -%}
          {%- assign nth = since | modulo: every -%}
          {% if at >= 0 and at <= 1000 and nth == 0 %}
            <span class="t-xs" style="position: absolute; top: {{ at | divided_by: 10.0 }}%; left: 0;
                        width: {{ gutter | minus: 6 }}px; text-align: right;
                        transform: translateY(-50%); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums">{{ hour }}</span>
          {% endif %}
        {% endfor %}

        <div style="position: absolute; top: 0; bottom: 0; left: {{ gutter }}px; right: 0">
          {% for hour in (first_hour..last_hour) %}
            {%- assign at = hour | times: 60 | minus: open | times: 1000 | divided_by: span -%}
            {% if at >= 0 and at <= 1000 %}
              <div style="position: absolute; top: {{ at | divided_by: 10.0 }}%; left: 0; right: 0;
                          border-top: 1px solid var(--ink)"></div>
            {% endif %}
          {% endfor %}

          {%- assign now_at = now_mins | minus: open | times: 1000 | divided_by: span -%}
          {% if now_at >= 0 and now_at <= 1000 %}
            <div style="position: absolute; top: {{ now_at | divided_by: 10.0 }}%; left: 0; right: 0; height: 3px;
                        background: var(--ink)"></div>
          {% endif %}

          {% for event in day.events %}
            {%- assign from = event.start_minutes | minus: open -%}
            {%- assign until = event.end_minutes | minus: open -%}
            {%- if until > 0 and from < span -%}
              {%- if from < 0 %}{% assign from = 0 %}{% endif -%}
              {%- if until > span %}{% assign until = span %}{% endif -%}
              {%- assign top = from | times: 1000 | divided_by: span -%}
              {%- assign tall = until | minus: from | times: 1000 | divided_by: span -%}
              {%- assign block_px = until | minus: from | times: track_h | divided_by: span -%}
              {%- assign lane_w = 100 | divided_by: event.lanes -%}
              {%- assign lane_at = event.lane | times: lane_w -%}
              {%- assign done = false -%}
              {%- if event.end_minutes <= now_mins %}{% assign done = true %}{% endif -%}
              {%- assign live = false -%}
              {%- if done == false and event.start_minutes <= now_mins %}{% assign live = true %}{% endif -%}

              <div style="position: absolute; top: {{ top | divided_by: 10.0 }}%; height: {{ tall | divided_by: 10.0 }}%;
                          left: {{ lane_at }}%; width: calc({{ lane_w }}% - 3px);
                          min-height: 10px; overflow: hidden;
                          border: 2px solid var(--ink); padding: 1px 5px;
                          {% if live %}border-left-width: 7px; padding-left: 4px;{% endif %}
                          {% if done %}background: repeating-linear-gradient(45deg, var(--paper) 0 4px, var(--ink) 4px 5px)
                      {% else %}background: var(--paper){% endif %}">
                {% if block_px >= 36 %}
                  <span class="t-xs t-bold" style="display: block; line-height: 1.15">{{ event.start }}</span>
                  <span class="t-xs truncate" style="display: block; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.2">{{ event.title }}</span>
                  {% if block_px >= 66 and extension.values.show_location != false and event.location != blank %}
                    <span class="t-xs truncate" style="display: block; font-weight: 400">{{ event.location }}</span>
                  {% endif %}
                {% elsif block_px >= 16 %}
                  {%- comment %} Too short for two lines: the time and as much
                    of the title as the width carries, on one. Shorter than
                    this and it carries none at all and is filled in instead -
                    a quarter of an hour is six pixels of a twelve-hour day,
                    and six pixels of clipped type reads as a broken screen
                    rather than as a short meeting. {% endcomment -%}
                  <span class="truncate" style="display: block; line-height: 1; font-size: 10px; font-weight: 700;
                               {% if done %}background: var(--paper){% endif %}">
                    {{ event.start }} {{ event.title }}
                  </span>
                {% endif %}
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          {% endfor %}
        </div>

        {% if now_at >= 0 and now_at <= 1000 %}
          <div style="position: absolute; top: {{ now_at | divided_by: 10.0 }}%; left: {{ gutter | minus: 8 }}px;
                      transform: translateY(-50%); width: 0; height: 0;
                      border-top: 5px solid transparent; border-bottom: 5px solid transparent;
                      border-left: 7px solid var(--ink)"></div>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  {% comment %}
    Where another extension gets to say something on this screen. Glyphs like
    dashboard warning lights, with the loudest one's words beside them when the
    box is wide enough to carry them.
  {% endcomment %}
  {% if notices.size > 0 %}
    <div class="notice-strip">
      {% for notice in notices %}
        {% if notice.overflow %}
          <span class="notice notice--more">+{{ notice.overflow }}</span>
        {% else %}
          <span class="notice notice--{{ notice.level }}" title="{{ notice.text }}">
            <span class="i i-{{ notice.icon }}"></span>
          </span>
        {% endif %}
      {% endfor %}

      {% if shape.wide and notices[0].text != blank %}
        <span class="notice-said">{{ notices[0].text }}</span>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  {% endif %}
</div>
